  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A materials list can record requested quantities and which garden activity needs them.\", \"decision\": \"How should shared material requests be combined?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteers jointly review activities and material quantities before adding a combined request to the list. Demand and allocation are settled in one discussion.\nVolunteers list materials by activity, and the coordinator combines matching requests before ordering. Activity plans determine the total request.\nThe coordinator posts available material quantities, and volunteers divide them among activities. Activity allocations begin from the supply already obtainable."
    }
  ],
